    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0427" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg255"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111N39/48</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-15T00:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 15, 1917, midnight</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received April 16, 6.45 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. Carranza declared before Congress to-night that Mexico would observe strict
                    neutrality in the present war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
